1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:04,079
Today I'll show you how SOMA AI helps you plan a vegetable garden:

2
00:00:04,079 --> 00:00:09,800
from a few layout ideas to raised beds you can really build, with drawings, a cut list and a shopping list.

3
00:00:13,150 --> 00:00:13,908
We use SOMA.

4
00:00:13,908 --> 00:00:18,080
It's free and open source, and you can download it at somacad.app.

5
00:00:19,030 --> 00:00:20,553
SOMA itself is free.

6
00:00:20,553 --> 00:00:23,142
For SOMA AI you bring your own AI:

7
00:00:23,142 --> 00:00:25,960
a ChatGPT subscription or an API key.

8
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:31,495
We start with a new model, saved as Garden plot.

9
00:00:31,495 --> 00:00:34,304
In the SOMA AI tab I pick the model:

10
00:00:34,304 --> 00:00:35,240
GPT-6.1 Sol.

11
00:00:42,750 --> 00:00:46,160
I want a few concepts to compare, so I turn the effort up to High.

12
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:53,035
Then I describe my garden in plain words:

13
00:00:53,035 --> 00:00:58,269
a free area of six by four metres for vegetables, with the water tap in one corner.

14
00:00:58,269 --> 00:01:04,260
I ask for a few layout ideas with raised beds, paths and maybe a compost spot, so I can choose.

15
00:01:07,517 --> 00:01:10,440
SOMA AI first reads its notes on how to work in SOMA.

16
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:15,237
Then it builds three layouts side by side, and looks at its own pictures to check them.

17
00:01:15,237 --> 00:01:17,167
After about six minutes it is done.

18
00:01:18,117 --> 00:01:26,733
Here are the three concepts for the six by four metre plot, each with raised beds, paths, a compost spot and the tap in the front left corner.

19
00:01:26,733 --> 00:01:31,527
A has four beds, B three long rows, and C is a U shape around a wide courtyard.

20
00:01:33,917 --> 00:01:37,804
The beds are 45 centimetres high, and the compost spot is 80 by 80.

21
00:01:37,804 --> 00:01:41,807
It also says honestly that sun and shade still need checking on site.

22
00:01:46,050 --> 00:01:48,746
Then it asks which layout I want to develop.

23
00:01:48,746 --> 00:01:49,297
I take B:

24
00:01:49,297 --> 00:01:54,260
three identical long beds with straight paths, good for rows and simple watering.

25
00:01:55,317 --> 00:01:56,913
Now it shows B on its own:

26
00:01:56,913 --> 00:02:02,499
three beds of one by two and a half metres, 45 centimetres high, with 70 centimetre aisles.

27
00:02:02,499 --> 00:02:06,305
The compost sits at the back right, the tap at the front left.

28
00:02:07,950 --> 00:02:10,672
The other concepts stay in the model under Show layout.

29
00:02:10,672 --> 00:02:14,880
And it reminds me to check that the tap corner and the entrance match my real garden.

30
00:02:16,617 --> 00:02:18,071
Now the beds themselves.

31
00:02:18,071 --> 00:02:22,554
I ask SOMA AI to work out one of them in detail, so I can really build it:

32
00:02:22,554 --> 00:02:26,189
boards, posts, standard screws, and a liner if it needs one.

33
00:02:26,189 --> 00:02:30,187
Plus a cut list, a shopping list and assembly steps with drawings.

34
00:02:36,050 --> 00:02:40,479
SOMA AI reads up on joints, strength and drawings, then asks two questions:

35
00:02:40,479 --> 00:02:43,314
which timber to use, and what the bed stands on.

36
00:02:43,314 --> 00:02:47,211
I let it pick new timber to buy, and my beds stand on garden soil.

37
00:02:49,317 --> 00:02:51,622
Then SOMA AI works for about 38 minutes.

38
00:02:51,622 --> 00:02:59,287
It models every board and post, writes the build guide, makes the drawings, and looks at each sheet to check that it is easy to read.

39
00:03:00,237 --> 00:03:01,433
Here is the bed:

40
00:03:01,433 --> 00:03:09,729
two and a half metres by one, 45 centimetres high, three courses of 45 by 150 millimetre boards on eight posts.

41
00:03:09,729 --> 00:03:13,167
327 parts, down to every bolt, washer and nut.

42
00:03:14,184 --> 00:03:18,874
Instead of screws driven into end grain, it chose stainless M8 through-bolts.

43
00:03:20,017 --> 00:03:23,726
Two M10 tie rods with steel plates stop the long sides from spreading.

44
00:03:23,726 --> 00:03:28,707
And a loose liner keeps the soil off the timber, with the bottom left open to the garden soil.

45
00:03:32,651 --> 00:03:34,996
For building, it made eleven drawing sheets.

46
00:03:34,996 --> 00:03:36,541
They are in the Drawings tab.

47
00:03:42,518 --> 00:03:44,366
An overview with the main dimensions,

48
00:03:51,118 --> 00:03:53,168
a drilling drawing for every board and post,

49
00:03:59,718 --> 00:04:02,088
the assembly in four illustrated steps,

50
00:04:05,718 --> 00:04:08,345
and the cut list with the shopping list:

51
00:04:08,345 --> 00:04:15,176
eight boards of three metres, one four metre post, the bolts, nuts and washers, the liner, and the soil.

52
00:04:15,176 --> 00:04:18,328
That is for one bed, times three for the garden.

53
00:04:20,384 --> 00:04:21,245
And it is honest:

54
00:04:21,245 --> 00:04:27,221
check the real timber sizes and the long bolts before buying, and dry-assemble the first bed before cutting all three.

55
00:04:27,221 --> 00:04:29,298
Its strength checks are only preliminary.

56
00:04:31,051 --> 00:04:32,270
Last, the whole plot.

57
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:42,084
I ask SOMA AI to put all three beds into the garden, and to make a layout drawing with the beds, the paths, the compost spot and the water tap, with the main dimensions.

58
00:04:47,318 --> 00:04:50,210
This time SOMA AI works for about 14 minutes.

59
00:04:50,210 --> 00:04:55,288
It places the detailed beds, draws the plan, and checks it in its own pictures.

60
00:04:56,238 --> 00:05:04,208
Now all three detailed beds stand in the six by four metre plot, with the paths, the compost spot at the back, and the tap at the front left.

61
00:05:05,251 --> 00:05:08,181
The layout drawing is the new first sheet of the drawing pack.

62
00:05:09,131 --> 00:05:12,050
It shows the whole plot with the main dimensions:

63
00:05:12,050 --> 00:05:21,581
six by four metres, the three beds with their 70 centimetre aisles, 60 centimetre paths at the front and left, 90 at the back, and the compost spot of 80 by 80.

64
00:05:22,531 --> 00:05:26,450
A note says the tap position is assumed and should be confirmed on site.

65
00:05:26,450 --> 00:05:30,261
And it even marks where the tie rods make the aisle a little narrower.

66
00:05:31,211 --> 00:05:32,345
That is the garden:

67
00:05:32,345 --> 00:05:38,136
three concepts, a buildable raised bed with its drawings and lists, and a plan of the whole plot.

68
00:05:38,136 --> 00:05:39,390
No CAD skills needed:

69
00:05:39,390 --> 00:05:41,181
you just describe your garden.

70
00:05:42,131 --> 00:05:45,769
From an empty patch of garden to a plan you can build.

71
00:05:45,769 --> 00:05:47,722
SOMA is free and open source:

72
00:05:47,722 --> 00:05:49,541
download it at somacad.app.
